cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Dual Membrane and Korselt Colour-Blindness in Eisenstein Carmichael Ideals (Part XXXVIII, Arithmetic Geodynamics on the 6N Skeleton)"
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Ruqing
    affiliation: "GUT Geoservice Inc., Montreal, Quebec, Canada"
    email: ruqing@hotmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ruqing1963/6N-eisenstein-dual-membrane"
abstract: >-
  Lifting the one-dimensional 6N skeleton to its two-dimensional source, the
  Eisenstein integers Z[omega], we prove a dual membrane theorem: no Eisenstein
  Carmichael ideal is divisible by the ramified prime above 3 (norm 3) or the
  inert prime above 2 (norm 4). The two exclusions rest on independent
  valuations - a 3-adic congruence and a 2-adic parity - so that the removal of
  2 and 3 that defines the 6N skeleton in one dimension is, in two dimensions, a
  theorem. Above the membrane, the type-composition spectrum of Eisenstein
  Carmichael ideals (split versus higher inert factors) is statistically
  indistinguishable from the null model induced by the factor pool alone
  (pure-split fraction 0.663 versus 0.642), establishing that the Korselt
  criterion is colour-blind at the measured resolution.
keywords:
  - Carmichael ideals
  - Eisenstein integers
  - generalised Korselt criterion
  - Carmichael numbers
  - number rings
  - 6N skeleton
  - pseudoprimes
  - computational number theory
